"""Build the static GitHub Pages overview from checked-in design/cost artifacts."""
from pathlib import Path
from collections import defaultdict
import json,html
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
e=json.loads((ROOT/'materials/estimate.json').read_text());n=json.loads((ROOT/'model/native-readback.json').read_text())
money=lambda x:f'${x:,.0f}'
cats=defaultdict(lambda:[0,0])
for r in e['material_rows']:cats[r['category']][0]+=r['low_usd'];cats[r['category']][1]+=r['high_usd']
biggest=max(v[0] for v in cats.values())
bars=''.join(f'<div class="bar-row"><span>{html.escape(c)}</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar" style="width:{v[0]/biggest*100:.1f}%"></div></div><strong>{money(v[0])}–{money(v[1])}</strong></div>' for c,v in sorted(cats.items(),key=lambda p:-p[1][0]))
labor_preview='<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Approach</th><th>Paid labor</th><th>Owner hands-on work</th><th>Build time</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join(f'<tr><td>{html.escape(r["option"])}</td><td>{money(r["labor_low_usd"])}–{money(r["labor_high_usd"])}</td><td>{r["owner_hours_low"]:,}–{r["owner_hours_high"]:,} hours</td><td>{r["calendar_weeks_low"]}–{r["calendar_weeks_high"]} weeks</td></tr>' for r in e['labor_options'])+'</tbody></table></div>'
site=f'''<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Draft design study for a single-story earth-bermed ranch near Portal, Arizona. Imperial plans, Blender construction model, US materials and transparent cost estimates."><title>Portal Earthship · Draft home design</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/site.css?v=construction-2"></head>
<body><main>
<nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a class="brand" href="index.html">PORTAL / EARTHSHIP</a><a href="#plan">The plan</a><a href="#study">Construction study</a><a href="materials/costs.html">Materials & costs</a><a href="#files">Downloads</a><a href="https://github.com/shusain/portal-earthship-home-design">GitHub ↗</a></nav>
<header class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">PORTAL, ARIZONA · DRAFT A · {e['date']}</p><h1>A ranch home,<br>set into the earth.</h1><p class="lede">One level. Three bedrooms. A south-facing walk-out yard and a protected, earth-bermed north wall.</p><span class="status">Layout A selected · construction design in progress</span><div class="buttons"><a class="button" href="#plan">Explore the plan</a><a class="button secondary" href="materials/costs.html">US materials & costs</a></div></div><img src="review/exterior.png" alt="Native Blender rendering of the south-facing ranch facade, lightweight shed roof and earth berms" width="1600" height="1000"></header>
<div class="metrics"><article><span>Overall footprint</span><strong>64′ × 34′</strong></article><article><span>Gross enclosed area</span><strong>2,176 sq ft</strong></article><article><span>Conservative clear floor</span><strong>1,914 sq ft</strong></article><article><span>Rooms</span><strong>3 bed / 2 bath</strong></article></div>
<p class="notice">Draft concept, not for construction. The footprint includes walls; clear floor excludes wall bands and door thresholds. Earth berms, patio and roof overhangs are outside the enclosed area. The baseline has an exposed lightweight roof; soil over the roof is not included.</p>
<section id="plan"><p class="eyebrow">01 / ROOM-FIRST PLAN</p><h2>Daylight and escape at the open face.</h2><p>The living room and all bedrooms face the south yard. The kitchen and dining area join the west living space through an open gallery. Baths, laundry, storage and mechanical space occupy the rear band against the berm. A primary-suite vestibule connects the bedroom, bath and walk-in closet.</p><a href="plans/A-long-ranch.svg" aria-label="Open full selected floor plan"><img class="plan" src="plans/A-long-ranch.svg" alt="Selected A floor plan, dimensioned in feet and inches, with room areas, fixtures and door swings" width="1500" height="1050" loading="lazy"></a><div class="buttons"><a class="button secondary" href="plans/A-long-ranch.svg" download>Download SVG plan</a><a class="button secondary" href="plans/A-long-ranch-rooms.csv">Room schedule CSV</a><a href="plans/B-compact-ranch.svg">View compact alternative B</a></div><p class="small">A was selected on November 2, 2026. Alternative B remains available for comparison: 58′ × 37′, approximately 2,146 sq ft gross / 1,885 sq ft clear.</p></section>
<section id="study"><p class="eyebrow">02 / CONSTRUCTION STUDY</p><h2>One source, inspectable assemblies.</h2><p>The Blender study separates footings, slab, retaining walls, waterproofing, insulation, drainage, interior framing, roof, openings and fixtures. Four saved scenes support exterior, cutaway, plan and structural review. A 14-stage visibility sequence uses the same construction objects as the material takeoff.</p><div class="grid"><figure><img src="review/cutaway.png" alt="Furnished cutaway showing the front bedroom wing and rear service rooms" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1000"><figcaption>Furnished cutaway · source fixtures are planning reservations.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="review/structure.png" alt="Structural reservation view showing framing and roof-member bearing lines" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1000"><figcaption>Structure · member sizes, spans and connections require engineering.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="buttons"><a class="button" href="model/Earth-Groundship.blend" download>Download Blender study</a><a class="button secondary" href="review/construction.gif">Watch construction reveal</a><a href="review/floor-plan.png">Full-resolution top view</a></div><details><summary>Section, burial and drainage intent</summary><img class="plan" src="plans/section-and-site.svg" alt="South-north schematic section with open yard, approximately six-foot rear burial and separate drainage systems" loading="lazy" width="1500" height="950"><p>Assumes south-falling ground, suitable soils, a low water table and a location outside flood/erosion hazards. Upslope interception, roof runoff and footing drainage are separate systems. Final outlet, berm slopes and retaining-wall loads need the actual parcel.</p></details></section>
<section id="materials"><p class="eyebrow">03 / CONSTRUCTION MATERIALS, LABOR & TIME</p><h2>What it takes to build the house.</h2><p>Land and off-grid power are already acquired. House wiring, protection and the existing-power interface remain included; new PV, battery, generator or utility-extension purchases are excluded.</p><div class="metrics"><article><span>House construction materials</span><strong>{money(e['material_low_usd'])}–{money(e['material_high_usd'])}</strong></article><article><span>Hired trade labor</span><strong>{money(e['labor_low_usd'])}–{money(e['labor_high_usd'])}</strong></article><article><span>Machinery / formwork / pump / lift</span><strong>{money(e['equipment_low_usd'])}–{money(e['equipment_high_usd'])}</strong></article><article><span>Hired-crew build time</span><strong>{e['calendar_weeks_low']}–{e['calendar_weeks_high']} weeks</strong></article></div><p><b>Reference direct construction: {money(e['overall_low_usd'])}–{money(e['overall_high_usd'])}</b> with owner-managed hired trades. Freight, tax, fees and contingency are listed separately. Optional patio, septic, off-house water source and long service trenches are outside the house headline.</p><h3>Compare labor approaches</h3>{labor_preview}<p class="small">Hours and billable trade rates are authored estimates, not contractor quotes. Crew count converts person-hours to working time; the schedule accounts for dependencies, overlapping trade crews, waiting and a 2–4 week buffer. Starts after permits and long-lead procurement; water/septic availability can still affect occupancy.</p><h3>House materials by category</h3><div class="budget-chart" aria-label="House material cost ranges by category">{bars}</div><div class="buttons"><a class="button" href="materials/costs.html">Materials, labor & schedule</a><a class="button secondary" href="materials/labor-and-schedule.csv">Trade hours & timing CSV</a><a href="materials/us-purchasing-and-costs.csv">US purchasing CSV</a></div><p>US stock throughout: dressed 2×4 is 1½″ × 3½″, dressed 2×6 is 1½″ × 5½″, studs at 16″ on center. Supplier benchmarks, allowances, waste and stock-pack rounding remain explicit. Lumber quantities are budgeting equivalents, not a cut list.</p></section>
<section><p class="eyebrow">04 / EVIDENCE & NEXT DECISIONS</p><h2>Checked geometry, open engineering.</h2><div class="grid"><div><h3>Checks completed</h3><ul><li>Room coverage, shared-wall ownership and semantic SVG readback.</li><li>Full conservative door-swing checks and fixture containment.</li><li>Connected 30″ furnished walking envelope and access at both bed sides and foot.</li><li>{n['unique_original_components']:,} original model components, closed positive-volume meshes and unit scales.</li><li>Four saved scenes and all 14 reveal stages verified after reopening the native file.</li></ul><p><a href="model/native-readback.json">Native validation receipt</a> · <a href="plans/A-long-ranch-routes.json">Furnished routes</a> · <a href="plans/negative-checks.json">Source rejection checks</a></p></div><div><h3>Before permit development</h3><ul><li>Confirm parcel, survey, flood/erosion status, soil and groundwater.</li><li>Engineer retaining walls, reinforcement, foundations, transfer beam and roof.</li><li>Coordinate 36″ nominal doors with actual prehung rough openings and hardware.</li><li>Complete daylight, ventilation, thermal, waterproofing and utility design.</li><li>Separate mechanical/pantry storage, review suite privacy and obtain local supplier/installer quotes.</li></ul><p>Cochise County adopted 2024 residential codes effective September 1, 2026, with 2023 NEC and retained 2012 IECC, subject to local amendments. <a href="https://cochise.az.gov/m/newsflash/Archive/Item/441?arcId=796">County adoption notice</a>.</p></div></div><p class="small">The 30″ walking envelope is a study input, not an accessibility certification. Nominal ceiling datum is 9′; the schematic dropped transfer beam reaches approximately 7′10″ underside locally. No structural, drainage or full code approval is implied.</p><a href="research/code-and-site-basis.md">Read the code and site research</a></section>
<section id="files"><p class="eyebrow">05 / PROJECT FILES</p><h2>Review, download, revise.</h2><div class="download-list"><a href="model/Earth-Groundship.blend" download>Blender model<small>Four scenes + construction timeline</small></a><a href="plans/A-long-ranch.svg" download>Selected floor plan<small>SVG · dimensions in feet / inches</small></a><a href="plans/section-and-site.svg" download>Section / site intent<small>Schematic burial and drainage</small></a><a href="materials/costs.html">Materials and costs<small>House materials, labor and build time</small></a><a href="materials/bill-of-materials.csv">Measured takeoff CSV<small>Net model quantities + allowances</small></a><a href="materials/us-purchasing-and-costs.csv">US purchasing CSV<small>Stock units, costs and source links</small></a><a href="materials/labor-and-schedule.csv">Trade labor / schedule CSV<small>Hours, crew sizes and dependencies</small></a><a href="materials/labor-options.csv">Labor options CSV<small>Hired trades, owner assistance and GC</small></a><a href="materials/overall-budget.csv">Direct construction CSV<small>Materials, hired labor and equipment</small></a><a href="https://github.com/shusain/portal-earthship-home-design">Source repository<small>Scripts, evidence and reproduction notes</small></a></div></section>
<footer>Portal Earthship Home Design · Draft A · Updated {e['date']} · All costs USD · <a href="https://github.com/shusain/portal-earthship-home-design/blob/main/README.md">Project notes</a></footer>
</main></body></html>'''
